## LEGAL PAGES

Build these five routes as static pages fetching content from `legal_pages` table:

- `/privacy` — Privacy Policy (Kenya DPA 2019 compliant)
- `/terms` — Terms of Service (includes medical disclaimer, no refunds, coins have no cash value)
- `/guidelines` — Community Guidelines (short, human, Instagram-style)
- `/data-deletion` — Data Deletion (how to delete account, what gets deleted, 7-year payment retention per Kenyan tax law)
- `/cookies` — Cookie Notice (essential auth cookies + PostHog analytics, toggle in Profile)

Seed real content for all five in the migration — no placeholders. Admin can edit from panel.

Link them in:
- Login footer: "By continuing, you agree to [Terms] and [Privacy Policy]."
- Signup checkbox: "I am 18+ and agree to [Terms], [Privacy Policy], [Guidelines]."
- Profile → Legal section
- Community pinned banner: "Be kind. No patient names. [Read guidelines]"
- Footer on legal pages

On signup, save consent to `users.metadata`: `terms_accepted_at`, `privacy_accepted_at`, `guidelines_accepted_at`, `terms_version`, `age_confirmed`.

